{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1575616359,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI4NjAzNzk2MDE="},"added":["UX"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"5251a8cf1239b834eec2d241c5de46425d3a2cbe"},"timestamp":1575643510,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2MjU5ODQ3Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3901#issuecomment-562598472"},"message":"I tried to download something manually, so I could test, if the connection to the s3-bucket is possible in general.\nRunning:\n```\n\u003e aws s3 cp s3://hcp-openaccess/HCP_1200/123420/T1w/ribbon.nii.gz ../rehab_hcp/tmp/ribbon.gz\n```\njust downloads the file, I can open it and it works fine.\n\nThen I tried this again with:\n```\ndatalad addurls code/tmp/123420.csv '{original_url}?versionId={version}' '{subject}//{filename}'\n```\n[WARNING] Not creating subdataset at existing path: 123420 \n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /data/project/rehab_hcp/123420/MNINonLinear \ncreate(ok): 123420/MNINonLinear (dataset)                                                                 \n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /data/project/rehab_hcp/123420/T1w \ncreate(ok): 123420/T1w (dataset)                                                                          \n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /data/project/rehab_hcp/123420/unprocessed \ncreate(ok): 123420/unprocessed (dataset)                                                                  \nAdding URLs (10352 failed):  65%|█████████████████████▎           | 10.4k/16.1k [00:50\u003c00:13, 414 Files/s]","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1575875404,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2MzA5NTk2NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3901#issuecomment-563095964"},"message":"### Replication on a different system with latest master\n\n```\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp % datalad create s3test\n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/s3test \ncreate(ok): /tmp/s3test (dataset)                                                            \n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp % cd s3test\n\n# basic credential setup is functional\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/s3test (git)-[master] % s3cmd get s3://hcp-openaccess/HCP_1200/123420/T1w/ribbon.nii.gz tmp_plain.nii.gz \ndownload: 's3://hcp-openaccess/HCP_1200/123420/T1w/ribbon.nii.gz' -\u003e 'tmp_plain.nii.gz'  [1 of 1]\n 586704 of 586704   100% in    1s   472.78 kB/s  done\n\n# `download-url` downloads successfully, but fails to `addurl`\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/s3test (git)-[master] % datalad download-url s3://hcp-openaccess/HCP_1200/123420/T1w/ribbon.nii.gz -O tmp.nii.gz\n[INFO   ] Downloading 's3://hcp-openaccess/HCP_1200/123420/T1w/ribbon.nii.gz' into '/tmp/s3test/tmp.nii.gz' \n[INFO   ] S3 session: Connecting to the bucket hcp-openaccess with authentication \ns3://hcp-openaccess/HCP_1200/123420/T1w/ribbon.nii.gz:  11%| | 65.5k/587k [00:00\u003c00:01, 332kBs3://hcp-openaccess/HCP_1200/123420/T1w/ribbon.nii.gz:  34%|▎| 197k/587k [00:00\u003c00:00, 397kB/s3://hcp-openaccess/HCP_1200/123420/T1w/ribbon.nii.gz:  67%|▋| 393k/587k [00:00\u003c00:00, 518kB/                                                                                             download_url(ok): /tmp/s3test/tmp.nii.gz (file)\nadd(ok): tmp.nii.gz (file)\nsave(ok): . (dataset)\n[WARNING] Registering /tmp/s3test/tmp.nii.gz with s3://hcp-openaccess/HCP_1200/123420/T1w/ribbon.nii.gz failed: AnnexBatchCommandError: command 'addurl'\nError, annex reported failure for addurl (url='s3://hcp-openaccess/HCP_1200/123420/T1w/ribbon.nii.gz'): {'command': 'addurl', 'success': False, 'error-messages': ['  while adding a new url to an already annexed file, failed to verify url exists: s3://hcp-openaccess/HCP_1200/123420/T1w/ribbon.nii.gz'], 'file': 'tmp.nii.gz'} [annexrepo.py:add_url_to_file:1878] \naction summary:\n  add (ok: 1)\n  download_url (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/s3test (git)-[master] % git annex whereis tmp.nii.gz\nwhereis tmp.nii.gz (1 copy) \n        ebf94ddf-e703-448c-b560-ddaf366c249c -- mih@meiner:/tmp/s3test [here]\nok\n```\n\nThis is a `download-url` bug, as the command gives exit code zero.\n\nIn any case, the download itself went fine (again confirming that the credential setup is functional):\n\n```\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/s3test (git)-[master] % md5sum *.gz\nd1edabbf0885312bc5967e0f559a525c  tmp.nii.gz\nd1edabbf0885312bc5967e0f559a525c  tmp_plain.nii.gz\n```\n\nNow same via `addurls`:\n\n```\n(datalad3-dev) 130 mih@meiner /tmp/s3test (git)-[master] % cat ../tbl.csv\noriginal_url,filename\ns3://hcp-openaccess/HCP_1200/123420/T1w/ribbon.nii.gz,tmp_addurls.nii.gz\n\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/s3test (git)-[master] % datalad addurls ../tbl.csv '{original_url}' '{filename}'\naddurls(error): /tmp/s3test/tmp_addurls.nii.gz (file) [AnnexBatchCommandError: command 'addurl'\nError, annex reported failure for addurl (url='s3://hcp-openaccess/HCP_1200/123420/T1w/ribbon.nii.gz'): {'command': 'addurl', 'success': False, 'error-messages': [], 'file': 'tmp_addurls.nii.gz'} [annexrepo.py:add_url_to_file:1878]]\n```\n\nInconclusive error message (`-l debug` doesn't add relevant info), nothing downloaded was placed into the dataset. I suspect that `addurls` is able to actually catch the error of `git annex addurl` and stops.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1575876683,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2MzEwMjI4MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3901#issuecomment-563102280"},"message":"### Solution\n\nEnable the datalad special remote.\n\n```\n% git annex initremote datalad type=external externaltype=datalad encryption=none autoenable=true\ninitremote datalad ok\n(recording state in git...)\n\n% datalad download-url s3://hcp-openaccess/HCP_1200/123420/T1w/ribbon.nii.gz -O tmp2.nii.gz\n[INFO   ] Downloading 's3://hcp-openaccess/HCP_1200/123420/T1w/ribbon.nii.gz' into '/tmp/s3test/tmp2.nii.gz' \n[INFO   ] S3 session: Connecting to the bucket hcp-openaccess with authentication \n...\ndownload_url(ok): /tmp/s3test/tmp2.nii.gz (file)\nadd(ok): tmp2.nii.gz (file)\nsave(ok): . (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (ok: 1)\n  download_url (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n\n% datalad addurls ../tbl.csv '{original_url}' '{filename}'                        \naddurl(ok): /tmp/s3test/tmp_addurls.nii.gz (file) [from datalad; to tmp_addurls.nii.gz]      \nadd(ok): /tmp/s3test/tmp_addurls.nii.gz (file)                                               \nmetadata(ok): /tmp/s3test/tmp_addurls.nii.gz (file)\nsave(ok): . (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (ok: 1)\n  addurl (ok: 1)\n  metadata (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n```\n\nThis necessity is neither mentioned in the docs of `download-url`, nor `addurls`. As it is only relevant for a subset of URLs (S3 in this case), I might be sufficient to catch the `annex addurl` error and issue a speculative message ala \"URLs of type ... require an enabled 'datalad' special remote for this dataset. Run: ...\", if no special remote is found enabled. It may need to be done for `download-url` and `addurls` separately, unless a common code path can be found (I did not figure one out at first attempt).","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1575876683,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDMyMTUzNTc3Ng=="},"target":"c231b2963b1258eeda23936287ccf3f71f696de951697049fb79490b08ebd5fe","message":"### Solution\n\nEnable the datalad special remote.\n\n```\n% git annex initremote datalad type=external externaltype=datalad encryption=none autoenable=true\ninitremote datalad ok\n(recording state in git...)\n\n% datalad download-url s3://hcp-openaccess/HCP_1200/123420/T1w/ribbon.nii.gz -O tmp2.nii.gz\n[INFO   ] Downloading 's3://hcp-openaccess/HCP_1200/123420/T1w/ribbon.nii.gz' into '/tmp/s3test/tmp2.nii.gz' \n[INFO   ] S3 session: Connecting to the bucket hcp-openaccess with authentication \n...\ndownload_url(ok): /tmp/s3test/tmp2.nii.gz (file)\nadd(ok): tmp2.nii.gz (file)\nsave(ok): . (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (ok: 1)\n  download_url (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n\n% datalad addurls ../tbl.csv '{original_url}' '{filename}'                        \naddurl(ok): /tmp/s3test/tmp_addurls.nii.gz (file) [from datalad; to tmp_addurls.nii.gz]      \nadd(ok): /tmp/s3test/tmp_addurls.nii.gz (file)                                               \nmetadata(ok): /tmp/s3test/tmp_addurls.nii.gz (file)\nsave(ok): . (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (ok: 1)\n  addurl (ok: 1)\n  metadata (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n```\n\nThis necessity is neither mentioned in the docs of `download-url`, nor `addurls`. As it is only relevant for a subset of URLs (S3 in this case), it might be sufficient to catch the `annex addurl` error and issue a speculative message ala \"URLs of type ... require an enabled 'datalad' special remote for this dataset. Run: ...\", if no special remote is found enabled. It may need to be done for `download-url` and `addurls` separately, unless a common code path can be found (I did not figure one out at first attempt).","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1575876607,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI4NjUyMDMwNjA="},"added":["severity-normal"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1575876620,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI4NjUyMDM2NzM="},"added":["documentation"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1576162446,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2NTAzOTk1OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3901#issuecomment-565039959"},"message":"I think overall we might like to have a registry of URLs 